<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Assembly (Bulgaria)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a> is the single-chamber parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, first convened under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarnovo-constitution">Tarnovo Constitution</a> of 1879. Grand National Assemblies have been called for constitutional changes, including the one that adopted the democratic constitution of 1991. Since then the 240-member assembly has elected the government in a parliamentary republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="National Assembly (Bulgaria)" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vortic Anvilring · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bulgaria_Parliament_2026.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Constitution of 1987, amended in 2012, made a semi-presidential republic: a president elected for five years without consecutive terms, a prime minister from the majority in the <b>National Assembly</b>, a two-chamber National Assembly and a modified Napoleonic Code.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-haiti">Republic of Haiti · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Reform also reached the religious communities: the Armenian National Constitution of 1863, 150 articles drafted by the Armenian intelligentsia, defined the powers of the Armenian Patriarch and set up an Armenian <b>National Assembly</b>.</blockquote><a href="/movement/tanzimat">Tanzimat · People</a></li><li><blockquote>Bulgaria is a parliamentary republic with a single-chamber <b>National Assembly</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></li></ul></section>
